8. Claim ledger

Proved or exact conditional on definitions. The selection-inflation identity \phi_{\mathrm{sel}} = \phi_V + \Delta(1-\pi_0) = \Lambda_0\phi_V and the equivalence chain. The eigenvalue bound n_{\mathrm{eff}}^{\lambda} = K/\lambda_{\max} \le K, with equality iff R=I, and n_{\mathrm{eff}}^{\lambda} \le n_{\mathrm{eff}}^{\mathrm{Kish}}. The corrected detection bound N \le \ln(1-\epsilon)/\ln q. Weakest-path dominance q_{\mathrm{sys}} = \min_p q_p. All-strong-path taint persistence. The separation of integrity and anteriority from completeness. The forking-refusal requirement for witnesses.

Cited empirical premises, bounded. Kohli's nine-judge, seven-family panel yields n_{\mathrm{eff}} = 2.18 [2.07, 2.31] with eigenvalue 2.16; the same-family gap is \approx 0.047 on MNLI and larger on RewardBench (arXiv:2605.29800). Awuni et al. report a same-family lift of 3.4–8.4 percentage points and global FPS 0.067 [0.053, 0.084] (arXiv:2605.01970 / family-audit preprint). The human-referenced effective sizes are \nu_H = 4.24–6.50 and \nu_{\mathrm{MSE}} = 2.30–3.75 (arXiv:2609.21277). Trojan Hippo reaches 85–100\% ASR with long dwell (arXiv:2605.01970). Sleeper poisoning reaches 99.8\% storage and 60–89\% conditional usage (arXiv:2605.15338). eTAMP reaches up to 32.5\% under stress conditions (arXiv:2604.02623). The 25-verifier 1.66 versus 1.00 result is a program-based experiment, not an LLM-judge result.

Conjecture. The accuracy paradox, with its two-premise decomposition and FDR-controlled test.

Open measurements. \Lambda_0 and \Delta per verifier on the target distribution; q_p per path; DAG completeness under paraphrase and multi-hop summarization; the latency distribution of the candidate observation channel; n_{\mathrm{eff}}^{\lambda} on the deployment panel with item bootstrap; the per-class ASR ceilings; the effectiveness of taint-margin escalation; and the self-consolidation rate.

Closed since the prior version. The detection-bound arithmetic (corrected), the one-strong-edge persistence claim (replaced), the \min\{\text{Kish},\text{eigenvalue}\} redundancy (reduced to the eigenvalue bound), the Test B null (replaced with the three-arm plausibility-stratified design), the \mathrm{Alg}\,\Lambda_0 power example (recomputed at 0.55–0.65), and the treatment of family labels (demoted to prior).

