Appendix F. Schema Invariants and Transition Predicates

All of Appendix F is [DESIGN]: these are specifications that a harness would enforce. No harness exists.

F.1 Claim schema

If status == SUPPORTED, evidence_refs is non-empty and every referenced Evidence has reliability in \{HIGH, MEDIUM\}. If judge_ref != null, judge_ref.lambda0_table_version refers to a table whose calibration set has drift below the pre-registered threshold at claim time, and judge_ref.calibration_run_id refers to a run whose PreRegistration is signed and whose \tau_{\text{task}} is not exceeded by the claim's \mathrm{UCB}(\phi_{\mathrm{sel}}). status_procedure_version matches the procedure used.

F.2 State-bound authorization grant

controller_signature verifies. expiry is in the future at EXECUTING. arguments_hash matches the emitted call. state_basis_hash matches the recomputed hash of the decision-relevant logged state at dispatch; a mismatch invalidates the grant and returns the action to AWAITING_AUTH. policy_version matches current policy. decision == ALLOW iff the applied policy rule evaluates to ALLOW for the permissions and target.

F.3 Execution event

matching_grant refers to an AuthorizationGrant with decision == ALLOW, unexpired, and a matching state_basis_hash. effect_receipt.gateway_signature verifies. observer_ref refers to an observation channel that recorded an effect with matching effect_digest; if no such record exists, the event is NOT_VERIFIABLE. event_hash = H(previous_hash, canonical_serialize(e_k \setminus \{event_hash\})).

F.4 Memory candidate

taint equals the join over derivation_parents of w \otimes t(\text{parent}), with write-time origin binding preventing any later reduction. If consolidation_decision == APPROVED and the candidate will justify a sensitive action, taint <= TRUSTED. If taint_margin_min < delta_margin, human_approver is non-null before APPROVED. Retrieval context at generation time is present in derivation_parents; its absence is a schema violation.

F.5 Transition predicates

PLANNING → TASK_READY: mandate signed, budgets set, acceptance test and allowed tool present. TASK_READY → AWAITING_AUTH: an action descriptor has been produced and its target tool is allowed. AWAITING_AUTH → EXECUTING: a grant exists with decision == ALLOW, unexpired, matching arguments_hash, matching state_basis_hash, matching policy_version. EXECUTING → VERIFYING: an execution event has been emitted with a valid receiver-signed receipt and an observer_ref recording the effect. VERIFYING → SUPPORTED: the evidence pipeline returns SUPPORTED and the verifier's \mathrm{UCB}(\phi_{\mathrm{sel}}) is below \tau_{\text{task}}. VERIFYING → CONTRADICTED / CONFLICT / UNKNOWN: as returned. Any → BLOCKED: a safety predicate fails (unauthorized action attempted, taint above threshold for a sensitive action, witness liveness or refusal-contract failure, or \mathrm{UCB}(\phi_{\mathrm{sel}}) exceeds \tau_{\text{task}}). Any → NOT_VERIFIABLE: the observation channel cannot confirm the effect within the damage window. No predicate contains an LLM invocation.

